191-### 2.7 Primary-skill reroute cue
192-
193:Reroute the primary skill when the problem shape changes:
194-- from `coding-core` to `orchestration-control` when coordination, async lifecycle, or delegated integration becomes the main problem rather than incidental implementation
195-- from `design-analysis` to `grounded-research` when the work is no longer mainly comparison but mainly evidence acquisition or provenance resolution
196:- from any primary skill to `eval-ops` when the real question becomes release gating, regression judgment, or monitored continuation
197-- from `coding-core` or `grounded-research` to `design-analysis` when multiple credible paths now compete and route quality is the main decision
198-
199-Reroute rule:
200:- one primary skill at a time
201-- reroute when the center of gravity changes
202-- do not keep old structure alive once the new dominant problem is clear
--
420-## 6. Final Rule
421-
422:Use one primary skill.
423-Attach only the overlays that materially change the result.
424-Prefer compact control packets over ornamental structure.
